      "text": "{\"active_time\": {\"evidence\": \"Spend 16 to 18 hours a day either feeding or moving toward a source of food or water.\", \"source_url\": \"https://ucmp.berkeley.edu/mammal/mesaxonia/elephantidae.php\", \"value\": [\"diurnal\"]}, \"body_length_m\": {\"evidence\": \"\", \"source_url\": \"\", \"value\": {\"max\": 4.0, \"min\": 3.0}}, \"body_mass_kg\": {\"evidence\": \"Woolly mammoths were 9-11 feet tall when fully grown and weighed 4-6 tons.\", \"source_url\": \"https://ucmp.berkeley.edu/mammal/mesaxonia/elephantidae.php\", \"value\": {\"max\": 6000.0, \"min\": 4000.0}}, \"body_plan\": {\"evidence\": \"It walked on four legs and was about the same size as a modern African elephant.\", \"source_url\": \"https://museumstore.hmns.org/products/woolly-mammoth\", \"value\": [\"quadruped\"]}, \"breathing\": {\"evidence\": \"whales are mammals like us. They produce milk, give birth to live young, use their lungs to breathe air, and are warm-blooded\", \"source_url\": \"https://naturalhistory.si.edu/sites/default/files/media/file/whale-evolution-activity-facilitation-guide-v2.pdf\", \"value\": \"lungs\"}, \"breathing_detail\": \"Terrestrial placental mammal breathing air through nostrils and trunk into lungs; no gills.\", \"claimed_crosses\": [], \"climate\": {\"evidence\": \"The haemoglobin of the Woolly Mammoth was adapted to the cold, with three mutations to improve oxygen delivery around the body and prevent freezing.\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.jacksonvillezoo.org/woolly-mammoth\", \"value\": [\"polar\"]}, \"covering\": {\"evidence\": \"and a coat of dense, furry, short hair overlain by longer, bristly hair.\", \"source_url\": \"https://kids.britannica.com/kids/article/mammoth-and-mastodon/275651\", \"value\": \"fur\"}, \"diet\": {\"evidence\": \"So, how can we tell these extinct behemoth herbivores apart? It\\u2019s all in the head!\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.amnh.org/explore/news-blogs/mammoth-mastodon-differences\", \"value\": \"herbivore\"}, \"habitat\": {\"evidence\": \"roamed the tundra and steppe grasslands of Europe, Africa, Asia and North America.\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.si.edu/newsdesk/snapshot/berezovka-woolly-mammoth-flesh-jar\", \"value\": [\"grassland\", \"tundra\"]}, \"mouthparts\": {\"evidence\": \"Mammoths, on the other hand, had ridged teeth\\u2014ideal for grazing and grinding tough grasses into small bits, like modern elephants.\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.amnh.org/explore/news-blogs/mammoth-mastodon-differences\", \"value\": \"grinding teeth\"}, \"mouthparts_detail\": \"Four ridged hypsodont molars at a time, replaced up to six times in life; jaw moves forward then backward so enamel ridges grind coarse grasses and sedges; trunk used to gather grass and tusks to clear snow.\", \"movement\": {\"evidence\": \"It walked on four legs and was about the same size as a modern African elephant.\", \"source_url\": \"https://museumstore.hmns.org/products/woolly-mammoth\", \"value\": [\"walk\"]}, \"primary_locomotor_part\": {\"evidence\": \"It walked on four legs and was about the same size as a modern African elephant.\", \"source_url\": \"https://museumstore.hmns.org/products/woolly-mammoth\", \"value\": \"four legs\"}, \"visible_features\": {\"evidence\": \"Perfectly adapted to its cold environment, the woolly mammoth had small ears, a short, goatlike tail, and a coat of dense, furry, short hair overlain by longer, bristly hair. It had a humplike reserve of fat on its back. Its long, dexterous trunk was used to gather grass and leaves. Its tusks were about 16 feet (5 meters) long.\", \"source_url\": \"https://kids.britannica.com/kids/article/mammoth-and-mastodon/275651\", \"value\": [\"long curved tusks\", \"shaggy fur coat\", \"small ears\", \"long trunk\", \"shoulder hump\"]}}",
